From 40d4753d10f6cf1dd689f27bac72f0c54a76e608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 10:06:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/51] meson: a 'vi' window-system platform for
 VK_NN_vi_surface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 1 (Swapchain with no global state)
Why: Horizon's window system is VI, reached through libnx's NWindow.
 Vulkan's surface type for it is VK_NN_vi_surface, whose declarations in
 vulkan_vi.h and whose VkIcdSurfaceVi in vk_icd.h are both behind
 VK_USE_PLATFORM_VI_NN, and whose entry point vkCreateViSurfaceNN is
 generated from vk.xml only when that macro is defined. There was no
 -Dplatforms value that defines it, so no build of Mesa could contain a
 VI surface at all.
Evidence: mesa/src/vulkan/registry/vk.xml:22559 declares VK_NN_vi_surface
 with platform="vi"; mesa/include/vulkan/vk_icd.h:226 puts VkIcdSurfaceVi
 behind VK_USE_PLATFORM_VI_NN; and `grep -rn VK_USE_PLATFORM_VI_NN
 src/vulkan` at mesa-26.1.5 finds nothing that defines it. Configuring
 this tree with -Dplatforms=vi before this patch fails at
 meson.options:14 with "platforms is not one of the choices".
Upstream: yes — it adds a platform the registry already describes, and
 defines nothing conditional on Horizon. 'vi' is never selected by
 'auto': no host_machine.system() maps to it, so it must be asked for.
---
 meson.build            | 4 ++++
 meson.options          | 2 +-
 src/vulkan/meson.build | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index e5d2efd5c9d..b18037e9d6a 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -472,6 +472,10 @@ with_platform_wayland = _platforms.contains('wayland')
 with_platform_haiku = _platforms.contains('haiku')
 with_platform_windows = _platforms.contains('windows')
 with_platform_macos = _platforms.contains('macos')
+# Never reached by 'auto': there is no host_machine.system() that selects
+# it, so it is always asked for explicitly. VK_NN_vi_surface is the
+# Vulkan surface type for Horizon's VI compositor.
+with_platform_vi = _platforms.contains('vi')
 
 with_gfxstream_emulated_android = with_gfxstream_vk and with_platform_android and host_machine.system() == 'linux'
 if with_gfxstream_emulated_android
diff --git a/meson.options b/meson.options
index db4865324c2..099120b9cb0 100644
--- a/meson.options
+++ b/meson.options
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ option(
   type : 'array',
   value : ['auto'],
   choices : [
-    'auto', 'x11', 'wayland', 'haiku', 'android', 'windows', 'macos',
+    'auto', 'x11', 'wayland', 'haiku', 'android', 'windows', 'macos', 'vi',
   ],
   description : 'window systems to support. If this is set to `auto`, all ' +
                 'platforms applicable will be enabled.'
diff --git a/src/vulkan/meson.build b/src/vulkan/meson.build
index 614a33a47c6..81a7bfb902d 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -68,6 +68,12 @@ endif
 if with_platform_windows
   vulkan_wsi_list += '-DVK_USE_PLATFORM_WIN32_KHR'
 endif
+if with_platform_vi
+  # No dependency to add: the platform's window system is libnx, which
+  # the driver already links, and vulkan_vi.h needs nothing but the
+  # define to expose VK_NN_vi_surface.
+  vulkan_wsi_list += '-DVK_USE_PLATFORM_VI_NN'
+endif
 if with_platform_macos
   vulkan_wsi_list += '-DVK_USE_PLATFORM_MACOS_MVK'
   vulkan_wsi_list += '-DVK_USE_PLATFORM_METAL_EXT'
-- 
